iproute2: drop the informational #warning from the no-libmnl stub

When libmnl is not enabled, libnetlink.c compiles the two no-op
nl_dump_ext_ack*() stubs. The #else branch also emits
#warning "libmnl required for error support"; that is an informational
notice, not a defect: the OpenWrt package deliberately keeps libmnl
optional and neither stub needs extended error ack support.

Replace the #warning with a normal comment. No code or conditional
structure changes, so the produced objects are identical, and a clean
build no longer reports the 2 -Wcpp warnings.

--- a/lib/libnetlink.c
+++ b/lib/libnetlink.c
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 #else
-#warning "libmnl required for error support"
+/* Extended error ack support requires libmnl; use the no-op stubs below. */
 
 /* No extended error ack without libmnl */
 int nl_dump_ext_ack(const struct nlmsghdr *nlh, nl_ext_ack_fn_t errfn)
